TY  - THES
AU  - Cornelius, D. E.
TI  - Mormonism in Montana, 1847–1898
PB  - Montana State University (now the University of Montana)
PY  - 1962
UR  - #repositories
KW  - Theses
N1  - Cornelius, D. E. “Mormonism in Montana, 1847–1898.” Master’s thesis, Montana State University (now the University of Montana), 1962. Chapter 6, “Mormon Schismatics in Montana” (pp. 56–66), treats the Reorganized Church in Montana from 1868 and the Deer Lodge Valley Morrisites, drawing on his 1962 interviews with Henry Hendrickson and Agnes Staffanson and on Reorganized Church records. It dates the Lost Creek church to 1872 and the Race Track church to 1878, and describes the Lord’s House as it stood in 1962. Its account of the Utah years is secondhand and calls Kington Fort “Knight Fort.” His interview with Henry Hendrickson is listed under Repositories. Online
ID  - cornelius1962mormonism
ER  - 

