N1  - Wright, Julie A. “Mormon Movement to Montana.” Master’s thesis, University of Montana, 2004. Pages 33–38 treat the Montana Morrisites and the RLDS. Drawing on the Butte District manuscript history of the Northwestern States Mission (Church History Library), it reports Latter-day Saint missionaries’ visits to the Morrisites at Willow Glen in 1896 and at Racetrack about a year later. It also summarizes a family history of Niels R. Beck (see his page). Its brief account of 1862 places the siege at Manti; it took place at Kington Fort on the Weber River. Online
ID  - wright2004mormon
