N1  - Deer Lodge County History Group. In the Shadow of Mount Haggin. A Bicentennial “Heritage” project, 1975; the cover reads Under the Shadow of Mt. Haggin. Family histories of the upper Deer Lodge Valley. The Morgan Evans family (pp. 134–137), from the notes of Katherine Evans Wellcome, has Ann Evans coming to the valley in 1865 after about eight years in Utah, living in a dugout near Gregson Springs among “a small colony there, three or four families” (later on the same page, “four or five families”), and then homesteading Gwendale Farm, about four miles north, near the present Anaconda Country Club; it dates the move to the spring of 1875. It does not say whether the Evanses or their neighbors were Morrisites. Cited by Patrick F. Morris, Anaconda, Montana (1997). New
